From 4ea2c94faf5a586579c216b77cb7bb3f2d2d53dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <me@diegonmarcos.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 18:18:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(c3-infra-mcp): GHA trigger inputs, cross-repo target,
 rerun + run logs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

devops.workflows.gha_trigger could start a workflow but could not steer
one. Three gaps, all hit while trying to drive a real deploy from an
agent instead of a browser.

1. NO INPUT SUPPORT. It ran `gh workflow run <id> --repo … --ref main`
   with no -f/--field, so a workflow_dispatch input could never be sent.
   Any workflow gated on an input was unreachable.

2. WRONG REPO, AND NOT OVERRIDABLE. GH_REPO is hardcoded to
   <owner>/cloud, so every Android/APK ship workflow — which lives in the
   `unix` monorepo — was invisible to this MCP no matter what was passed.
   This was the gap that actually blocked driving a deploy; the missing
   inputs would not have mattered without it. `repo` is now a parameter.

3. NO RERUN, NO PER-RUN LOGS. A transient infrastructure failure (an
   upstream registry 401/5xx, an Actions cache outage) could be observed
   but not retried, and gha_errors only reaches the last 24h, so
   diagnosing any older run meant leaving the MCP for the web UI.

Added: `inputs`, `ref` and `repo` on gha_trigger; devops.workflows.gha_rerun
(defaults to --failed, so a flake does not re-pay for the whole matrix);
devops.workflows.gha_run_logs (one run by id, tailed to 400 lines because
a matrix log is megabytes).

Inputs are rejected for a bulk 'all' trigger rather than silently dropped:
inputs are per-workflow by definition, and thirty workflows quietly
ignoring one reads as success while doing nothing.

gh() spawns via execAsync with an argv ARRAY, so there is no shell to
inject into — but a key beginning with "-" would still be parsed by gh as
a flag, so input names are validated against [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_-]* and
values carrying newlines are refused.

Typechecked against the real dependency tree: 9 pre-existing errors before
this change, 9 after, none in the added code. The three that touch
workflows.ts are the long-standing safeRun return-type mismatch at line
26, shared with finops.ts and vps-ops.ts and untouched here.
